// @test: failing main()<String,E> reports untrapped failure instead of being swallowed
// @description: A failable main whose payload is a String lowers to a struct whose
//   payload element is itself a String ({ {ptr,len}, i8* }), which a fixed 2-element
//   shape heuristic misclassified as neither failable nor String — so the failure
//   was silently swallowed with exit 0. Detection now keys on the trailing error
//   pointer, so the untrapped failure is reported and the process exits non-zero.
// @category: error,main,failable,return
// @expect: fail
// @expect-error: UNTRAPPED FAILURE

main()<String> -> {
    fail<String>("boom")
    return "never"
}